= Validation set =

== Overview ==
A '''validation set''' is data excluded from direct model-parameter fitting and used during development to choose models, hyperparameters, thresholds, stopping points, preprocessing decisions, or other design choices.

Validation estimates guide development.

== Model selection ==
A validation set can be used to compare:

* architectures;
* regularization strengths;
* feature sets;
* hyperparameters;
* early-stopping checkpoints;
* decision thresholds.

Because those choices depend on validation performance, the final selected system is indirectly adapted to the validation set.

== Validation overfitting ==
Repeated experimentation can overfit the validation criterion.

If many alternatives are tried, the best observed validation score may partly reflect noise.

This is one source of [[Model selection bias]].

== Validation and testing ==
A [[Test set]] should remain independent of the development choices being evaluated.

If test results are repeatedly used to change the system, the test set has become another validation set in practice.

== Cross-validation ==
Cross-validation estimates development performance by rotating data through training and validation roles.

Nested cross-validation can separate inner model selection from outer performance estimation.

